<title>CHINA: TABLE-Seapower Resources net off 31.2 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Seapower Resources net off 31.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  4.3    vs 6.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   1.0    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 nil    vs 11.85 gain</p>
<p>    Net			   52.25  vs 75.96</p>
<p>    Turnover		    806.10 vs 628.67 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		Seapower Resources International Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 September 19-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  October 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Seapower Resources is involved in investment, cold-storage warehousing and property financing.</p>
<p>The turnover has been adjusted to HK$628.67 million from HK$628.74 million for the year ended March 31, 1996 following the auditors' comments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs 1.3 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
